      "text": "Polite. Professional. No inbox panic.\n\nHi VeeAy! Today we're turning one big job-search challenge into practical steps you can actually use. Keep this guide handy and try the small activity at the end.\n\nKnow when to follow up\n\nCheck the employer's instructions first. If there's no stated timeline, a single polite message after roughly one or two weeks may be reasonable.\n\nKeep it brief\n\nMention the role, your application date and continued interest. Ask for an update without pressure.\n\nMove forward either way\n\nTrack your follow-up and keep exploring other roles. Repeated messages rarely improve an application.\n\nREAL-WORLD EXAMPLE\n\nSubject: Follow-up on [Role] application\n\nHello [Name],\n\nI applied for the [Role] position on [Date] and wanted to follow up. I'm still interested and happy to provide additional information.\n\nThank you for your time.\n[Your Name]\n\nYOUR TINY WIN\n\nCheck your tracker and choose one appropriate follow-up date.\n\nVEEAYS PRO\n\nPro helps you manage application stages, notes and follow-up reminders in one place—especially useful when you're juggling multiple opportunities.\n\n₱499 / 30 days · No auto-renewal\n\nhttps://veeays.com/pro\n\nContinue exploring jobs\n\nhttps://veeays.com/jobs\n\nThe VeeAys Team\n\nVEEAYS WEB PORTAL SERVICE, 100 San Juan ACCFA, Cabanatuan City, Nueva Ecija, Philippines\n\nUnsubscribe from optional VeeAys emails: {{{UNSUBSCRIBE_URL}}}\n"
